==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Uniform Motion|12}}

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[One Horn]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 146.67~150 seconds<sup>4,400f~4,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Alpacky]] spawns after 126.67 seconds<sup>3,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], as well as [[Tiny Ancient Hunt (Combo)|Tiny Ancient Hunt]] for extra damage. As soon as the stage begins, start spamming either [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cats]], [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Rapper Cats]], or [[Ancient Egg: N206 (Special Cat)|Clam Cats]] to meatshield, and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] for sustained DPS. This strategy is most consistent with Rapper Cat, especially on {{2c}}. Bring [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]/[[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] for extra defense once Alpacky spawns, since it'll become difficult to hold your ground and damage Infernal Pegasus Deonil without them. As long as you don't get outrageously unlucky with Deonil Freezes, you'll find this to be quite easy.

